outputs.L1:
The present invention pertains to a homogeneous, solid, particulate composition based on urea ammonium sulphate, comprising urea ammonium sulphate together with a urease inhibitor of the phosphoric triamide type. The composition is further characterized in that one or more of the following conditions apply:

a) it contains 5 weight percent or less, relative to the total weight of the composition, of one or more alkaline or alkaline-forming inorganic or organic compounds capable of interacting with ammonium sulphate;

b) the phosphoric triamide-type urease inhibitor is present in solid particulate form;

c) an anticaking and/or moisture-repellent coating is applied to the urea ammonium sulphate particulate material.

The composition of the invention exhibits enhanced properties for reducing ammonia loss resulting from urease activity in soil, rendering it particularly well-suited for use as a fertilizer.

The invention further relates to a method for manufacturing a homogeneous, solid, particulate urea ammonium sulphate-based composition comprising urea, ammonium sulphate, and a urease inhibitor of the phosphoric triamide type—preferably N-(n-butyl) thiophosphoric triamide (nBTPT)—as well as to a composition or kit of parts comprising:

a) one or more alkaline or alkaline-forming inorganic compounds capable of interacting with ammonium sulphate;

b) the phosphoric triamide-type urease inhibitor in solid particulate or liquid form, preferably N-(n-butyl) thiophosphoric triamide (nBTPT);

c) optionally, one or more anticaking and/or moisture-repellent compounds.

outputs.L2:
This disclosure presents a uniform, granular solid formulation built around urea ammonium sulphate, which incorporates a phosphoric triamide-class urease inhibitor. This urea ammonium sulphate-based formulation is distinguished by satisfying at least one of the following conditions: a) the total content of alkaline substances or alkali-generating compounds (whether inorganic or organic) capable of reacting with ammonium sulphate does not exceed 5 weight percent of the overall composition; b) the phosphoric triamide-type urease inhibitor exists as a solid granular substance; c) the granular urea ammonium sulphate material carries a coating designed to prevent caking and/or repel moisture.

This inventive formulation demonstrates enhanced capability to minimize ammonia losses stemming from soil urease enzymatic action, making it especially well-suited for agricultural fertilizer applications.

Additionally, this disclosure encompasses a production process for creating such a uniform, granular, solid composition based on urea ammonium sulphate—containing urea, ammonium sulphate, and a phosphoric triamide-class urease inhibitor (with N-(n-butyl) thiophosphoric triamide, or nBTPT, being a particularly preferred choice). The disclosure also covers a kit-style composition made up of the following elements:

a) one or several alkaline compounds or substances capable of generating alkalinity, of inorganic origin, that can react with ammonium sulphate;

b) a phosphoric triamide-based urease inhibitor available in either solid granular or liquid form, with N-(n-butyl) thiophosphoric triamide (nBTPT) representing the preferred embodiment;

c) as an optional component, one or more substances that provide anticaking properties and/or moisture resistance.
